["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Know where the lungs and heart sit under the fur and fat, and you will not lose a bear. Know the fat, and you will not lose the meat.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cutaway of a black bear from the side. Lungs fill the front of the chest behind the shoulder. The heart sits low in the chest, just behind the elbow. A thin muscle wall, the diaphragm, separates the chest from the belly. Behind it are the liver, one simple stomach, and the gut. A thick fat layer lies under the hide, thickest in fall.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Inside a black bear (side view)</text><g transform=\"translate(180 170) scale(2)\"><path d=\"M-62 8 Q-70 -36 -32 -40 Q0 -36 34 -30 Q60 -24 60 6 Q40 32 -40 30 Q-62 28 -62 8 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><path d=\"M54 -26 L82 -20 L100 -10 Q104 -2 98 0 L74 6 Q58 4 54 -26 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"-50\" y=\"22\" width=\"13\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"22\" width=\"13\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><path d=\"M-62 8 Q-70 -36 -32 -40 Q0 -36 34 -30 Q60 -24 60 6 Q40 32 -40 30 Q-62 28 -62 8 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e0b84a\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><ellipse cx=\"30\" cy=\"-6\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"17\" fill=\"#e7a0a0\"/><ellipse cx=\"34\" cy=\"10\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#b02a2a\"/><path d=\"M12 -22 Q6 0 12 22\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><ellipse cx=\"2\" cy=\"4\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#7a3b2a\"/><ellipse cx=\"-16\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><ellipse cx=\"-38\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#e3b7a0\"/><path d=\"M62 -24 L66 -36 L72 -22 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b04040\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lungs</text><line x1=\"204\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Diaphragm</text><line x1=\"148\" y1=\"162\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stomach</text><line x1=\"62\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a07a10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fat</text><line x1=\"256\" y1=\"194\" x2=\"345\" y2=\"234\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"345\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b02a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heart: low</text><line x1=\"184\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"274\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Liver</text><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"274\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gut</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Heart sits low, behind the shoulder <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>One stomach. Thick fat in fall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Frame and claws, breathing, heart, digestion, fat through the year, the den body, lifespan, and what each means for the shot and the meat.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-01\">Chapter 1, Meet the animal</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-03\">Chapter 3, The senses</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Front paws compared. Black bear: short, strongly curved claws, rarely over about 3.8 cm (1.5 inches), built for climbing trees. Grizzly: long, straighter claws built for digging. Claws are visible only up close or in tracks.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Front claws: the hard clue</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"52\" width=\"186\" height=\"210\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"52\" width=\"186\" height=\"210\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"103\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black bear</text><text x=\"297\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grizzly</text><ellipse cx=\"103\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><circle cx=\"69\" cy=\"152\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M69 146 q -14 -12.0 -7.0 -24\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"146\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M86 140 q -14 -12.0 -7.0 -24\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"103\" cy=\"146\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M103 140 q -14 -12.0 -7.0 -24\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"146\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M120 140 q -14 -12.0 -7.0 -24\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"137\" cy=\"152\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M137 146 q -14 -12.0 -7.0 -24\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"297\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><circle cx=\"263\" cy=\"152\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M263 146 q -4 -26.0 -2.0 -52\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"280\" cy=\"146\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M280 140 q -4 -26.0 -2.0 -52\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"297\" cy=\"146\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M297 140 q -4 -26.0 -2.0 -52\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"314\" cy=\"146\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M314 140 q -4 -26.0 -2.0 -52\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"331\" cy=\"152\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M331 146 q -4 -26.0 -2.0 -52\" stroke=\"#d8d0c0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"103\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Short, curved</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">rarely over 3.8 cm</text><text x=\"297\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Long, straighter</text><text x=\"297\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">for digging</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Curved claws climb trees. Straight claws dig.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Flat footed (plantigrade), five toes, short curved claws <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Built to climb trees, not to dig <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the frame in detail</summary><ul><li>BC account <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>: \"a chunky body, small black eyes, a broad head, rounded ears, a short tail, and a fine, long pelage\"; feet \"flat soled (plantigrade), with naked pads and five toes with relatively short curved claws\".</li><li>Grizzlies have \"much longer claws that are adapted for digging, whereas the shorter, curved claws of black bears are well suited for tree climbing\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>A black bear can run equally fast uphill or downhill and is an excellent climber (75%, WildSafeBC). Lean bears can top 48 km/h (30 mph) (70%, North American Bear Center). You cannot outrun one (Tip).</li><li>Long fur hides the true outline of the body and legs. The chest is lower than it looks (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cutaway of a black bear from the side. Lungs fill the front of the chest behind the shoulder. The heart sits low in the chest, just behind the elbow. A thin muscle wall, the diaphragm, separates the chest from the belly. Behind it are the liver, one simple stomach, and the gut. A thick fat layer lies under the hide, thickest in fall.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Inside a black bear (side view)</text><g transform=\"translate(180 170) scale(2)\"><path d=\"M-62 8 Q-70 -36 -32 -40 Q0 -36 34 -30 Q60 -24 60 6 Q40 32 -40 30 Q-62 28 -62 8 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><path d=\"M54 -26 L82 -20 L100 -10 Q104 -2 98 0 L74 6 Q58 4 54 -26 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"-50\" y=\"22\" width=\"13\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"22\" width=\"13\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><path d=\"M-62 8 Q-70 -36 -32 -40 Q0 -36 34 -30 Q60 -24 60 6 Q40 32 -40 30 Q-62 28 -62 8 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e0b84a\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><ellipse cx=\"30\" cy=\"-6\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"17\" fill=\"#e7a0a0\"/><ellipse cx=\"34\" cy=\"10\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#b02a2a\"/><path d=\"M12 -22 Q6 0 12 22\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><ellipse cx=\"2\" cy=\"4\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#7a3b2a\"/><ellipse cx=\"-16\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><ellipse cx=\"-38\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#e3b7a0\"/><path d=\"M62 -24 L66 -36 L72 -22 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b04040\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lungs</text><line x1=\"204\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Diaphragm</text><line x1=\"148\" y1=\"162\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stomach</text><line x1=\"62\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a07a10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fat</text><line x1=\"256\" y1=\"194\" x2=\"345\" y2=\"234\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"345\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b02a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heart: low</text><line x1=\"184\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"274\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Liver</text><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"274\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gut</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Lungs fill the chest behind the shoulder <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>A muscle wall, the diaphragm, pumps them <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: breathing in detail</summary><ul><li>Like all mammals, a bear breathes with its diaphragm: the dome shaped muscle between the chest and belly pulls air in as it flattens (90%, basic mammal anatomy).</li><li>The lungs are the biggest target in the chest. A shot through both lungs collapses them; the bear runs on held oxygen for a short distance (75%, hunter education).</li><li>In the den, oxygen intake drops by half (90%, BC account).</li><li>Bright, frothy blood on a trail means lungs (70%, chapter 10).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 640\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"640\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black bear: where to aim</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(0,34)\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"2\" width=\"388\" height=\"186\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">1  Broadside</text><text x=\"388\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">best</text><rect x=\"211\" y=\"115\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"300\" y=\"115\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"183\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"76\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"178\" cy=\"75\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"92\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"262\" cy=\"96\" rx=\"73\" ry=\"29\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M207 73 Q229 58 258 69\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"262\" cy=\"96\" rx=\"82\" ry=\"38\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">hair line</text><rect x=\"218\" y=\"115\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"309\" y=\"115\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"246\" cy=\"97\" rx=\"25\" ry=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\"0.35\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"231\" cy=\"110\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"238\" cy=\"97\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"233\" y1=\"97\" x2=\"243\" y2=\"97\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"238\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"238\" y2=\"102\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"254\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">aim</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Halfway up, tight behind the shoulder.</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Heart sits low. Lungs reach past the middle.</text></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(0,228)\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"2\" width=\"388\" height=\"186\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">2  Quartering away</text><text x=\"388\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">good</text><rect x=\"233\" y=\"109\" width=\"13\" height=\"29\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"243\" y=\"111\" width=\"13\" height=\"29\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"203\" cy=\"86\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"73\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"199\" cy=\"72\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"187\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"272\" cy=\"96\" rx=\"53\" ry=\"29\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M233 73 Q248 58 269 69\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"301\" cy=\"102\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"28\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"117\" width=\"15\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"305\" y=\"119\" width=\"15\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"255\" cy=\"97\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\"0.35\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"271\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"231\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><circle cx=\"231\" cy=\"92\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><text x=\"227\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">far shoulder</text><circle cx=\"271\" cy=\"104\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"266\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"276\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"271\" y1=\"99\" x2=\"271\" y2=\"109\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"287\" y=\"109\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">aim</text><text x=\"388\" y=\"57\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">rump toward you</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Aim farther back than feels right.</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Bullet must cross both lungs to the far shoulder.</text></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(0,422)\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"2\" width=\"388\" height=\"186\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">3  Quartering to</text><text x=\"388\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">experienced only</text><rect x=\"230\" y=\"111\" width=\"13\" height=\"29\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"296\" y=\"109\" width=\"13\" height=\"29\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"272\" cy=\"96\" rx=\"53\" ry=\"29\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M233 73 Q248 58 269 69\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"239\" cy=\"100\" rx=\"19\" ry=\"28\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"205\" cy=\"84\" rx=\"21\" ry=\"17\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"214\" cy=\"67\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"199\" cy=\"66\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"184\" cy=\"86\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><rect x=\"239\" y=\"117\" width=\"15\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"305\" y=\"115\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"256\" cy=\"97\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\"0.35\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"242\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"285\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><circle cx=\"242\" cy=\"100\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"237\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"247\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"242\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"242\" y2=\"105\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"256\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">aim</text><rect x=\"306\" y=\"30\" width=\"78\" height=\"24\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"345\" y=\"47\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">WAIT</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Not recommended. Heavy shoulder, dense skull.</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Wait for broadside, near leg forward.</text></g>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"634\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shaded: lungs. Dark: heart. Orange: aim point. Not to scale.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Halfway up, tight behind the shoulder, near leg forward <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Lungs reach past the middle of the body <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: heart and vessels in detail</summary><ul><li>The heart sits low in the chest, behind the shoulder; the lungs reach past the middle of the body; the chest is compressed front to back and the shoulder sits farther forward than a deer's (70 to 85%, <a href=\"#/s/shot-placement\">shot placement</a>, from the IBEP (International Bowhunter Education Program) bear guide).</li><li>Fat is 2.5 to 5 cm thick and the hair adds 8 to 10 cm: the bear looks bigger than it is <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Everyone agrees: halfway up the body, tight behind the shoulder once the near leg steps forward, through both lungs. Vital zone about a 20 cm (8 in) circle <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>The big vessels run from the top of the heart along the underside of the spine. A shot high in the lungs can still cut them (Tip).</li><li>The leg and shoulder bones shield the heart and lungs when the near front leg is back in its stride; wait for the leg to step forward (70%, Virginia hunting tips adapted from the National Bowhunter Education Foundation).</li><li>Thick fur and fat soak up blood: bears often leave a thin blood trail (Tip, quick lesson).</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=30aA9u-hrD8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Bear SHOT Placement 101: What Hunters Get Wrong</b><small>Bears are built differently. Study the vitals before the hunt.<br>Cliff Gray, YouTube, 10 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Comparison of a deer gut and a black bear gut. A deer has a four chambered stomach that ferments plants. A black bear has one simple stomach and a short gut, like a carnivore. Bears digest grass poorly, so they seek rich, easy to digest food: berries, fish, insects and young animals.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bear gut vs deer gut</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"52\" width=\"186\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"52\" width=\"186\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"103\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Deer</text><text x=\"297\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black bear</text><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"130\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"118\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"160\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"190\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"103\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4 chambers, ferments</text><path d=\"M260 110 Q300 95 330 120 Q340 160 300 168 Q262 160 260 110 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M300 168 q20 10 0 20 q-20 10 0 20 q20 10 0 10\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"297\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 stomach, short gut</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Grass digests poorly: bears seek rich food</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">like berries, fish, insects, young animals.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A carnivore's gut that eats mostly plants <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>So it hunts rich, easy food <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: digestion in detail</summary><ul><li>Bears are \"classified as carnivores (meat eaters), but they are omnivorous\" and \"seek out low fibre, easily digestible foods\" (90%, BC account).</li><li>Plants are most of the diet: about 80% (75%, WildSafeBC). Plants dominate in spring and summer <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Because they digest fibre poorly, bears go for concentrated foods: spawning fish, dense berry patches, insects, newborn deer, elk and moose (90%, BC account).</li><li>What this means for you: find the richest food in season and you find the bear (Tip, chapter 7).</li><li>Gut care: one stomach and a short gut. Keep the gut whole when you field dress (Tip, chapter 10).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Line sketch of a black bear weight through the year. Weight falls through the winter in the den and keeps falling into late spring and early summer. It climbs fast from August to October during the fall feed, and peaks before the den. Bears can lose up to a quarter of their body weight while denned. The line shows the shape only, not exact kilograms.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weight through the year (shape only)</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text><text x=\"82\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text><text x=\"138\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text><text x=\"222\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"278\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text><text x=\"306\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O</text><text x=\"334\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">N</text><text x=\"362\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text><polyline points=\"54,170 82,190 110,205 138,218 166,222 194,214 222,200 250,180 278,140 306,110 334,100 362,120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"60\" width=\"96\" height=\"190\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".12\"/><rect x=\"334\" y=\"60\" width=\"56\" height=\"190\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".12\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">In den</text><text x=\"386\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\">Den</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Lowest: late spring</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Fall peak</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Den loss up to a quarter of body weight (90%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Lean in spring, fattest just before the den <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Fall bears may eat up to 20,000 calories a day <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the fat year in detail</summary><ul><li>About 20% heavier in fall than after the den (85%, Alaska Department of Fish and Game). Some agencies report 20 to 50% gains in fall <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>\"Only about six months to build up fat reserves for hibernation\" (90%, BC account).</li><li>Fall feeding frenzy: <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Hyperphagia\">Hyperphagia</button>, up to 20,000 calories a day (70%, WildSafeBC). Chapter 5 has the timing.</li><li>A fall bear carries a thick fat layer under the hide; a spring bear little (75%, hunting media).</li><li>Fat and a thick hide hold heat: skin a bear fast or the meat spoils (75%, Maryland Department of Natural Resources). Chapter 10.</li><li>Rendered fall bear fat makes good lard, if the bear ate berries, not fish (Tip, hunting media).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of two hearts. In summer a black bear heart beats about 55 times a minute; in the den it slows to about 14 a minute, with long pauses. The summer heart pulses 8 times while the den heart pulses twice. Then a caption: slow heart, slow burn, metabolism near 25 percent of normal.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heartbeats: summer vs den</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"48\" width=\"180\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Summer</text><g transform=\"translate(100 150)\"><g><path d=\"M0 24 C -44 -8 -28 -44 0 -24 C 28 -44 44 -8 0 24 Z\" fill=\"#b02a2a\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"1;1.25;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.15;0.4\" dur=\"1.1s\" repeatCount=\"8\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><text x=\"100\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 55 a minute</text><rect x=\"210\" y=\"48\" width=\"180\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">In the den</text><g transform=\"translate(300 150)\"><g><path d=\"M0 24 C -44 -8 -28 -44 0 -24 C 28 -44 44 -8 0 24 Z\" fill=\"#b02a2a\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"1;1.25;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.15;0.4\" dur=\"4.3s\" repeatCount=\"2\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><text x=\"300\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 14 a minute</text><g opacity=\"0\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"258\" width=\"360\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Slow heart, slow burn: metabolism near 25%</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"8.6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Heart slows from about 55 to 14 a minute. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Heart about 50 to 55 drops to 10 to 14 a minute (80 to 90%).</li></ul><ul><li>No eating, drinking, peeing or pooping for months <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Table of how a black bear body changes in the den. Heart rate drops from about 50 to 55 beats a minute to about 10 to 14. Metabolism drops to about 25 percent of normal. Body temperature falls only about 3 to 6 degrees Celsius. The bear does not eat, drink, urinate or defecate for months. It can lose up to a quarter of its body weight.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">In the den: the body slows down</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Summer</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Denned</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"74\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Heart</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50 to 55</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 to 14 a minute</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"116\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Metabolism</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 25%</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"158\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Body temp</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">normal</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 to 6 C lower</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"200\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eat, drink</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">yes</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">none for months</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"242\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weight</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fall peak</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a quarter lost</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: den physiology in detail</summary><ul><li>BC account <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>: heart rate \"drops from about 50 beats per minute to around 10\"; oxygen intake halves; body temperature drops by about 3°C; no eating, drinking, urinating or defecating; up to a quarter of body weight lost.</li><li>University of Alaska study (Tøien and others, Science 2011, via ScienceDaily) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>: metabolism fell to about 25% of normal; body temperature only 5 to 6°C lower, cycling between 30 and 36°C; heart from about 55 to about 14 beats a minute; metabolism stayed low for 2 to 3 weeks after den exit.</li><li>WildSafeBC: about 30% of body weight lost over winter <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>What it means: a spring bear is lean, slow to recover, and hungry. That is why spring hunting focuses on the first green food (Tip, chapter 7).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline of a black bear cub from the BC account. Mating early June to mid July. Delayed implantation: the embryo implants in October or November. Cubs born in the den in January or February, hairless and about 400 grams. Leave the den in spring at 2 to 5 kilograms. Weaned July to September. Den with the mother the first winter. On their own by the middle or end of their second spring.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">From mating to a bear on its own</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"66\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"91\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Jun to Jul</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Mating</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"99\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"107\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Oct to Nov</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Embryo implants</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"132\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"157\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Jan to Feb</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Born, about 400 g</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"165\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Apr to May</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Out, 2 to 5 kg</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"198\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"223\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Jul to Sep</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weaned</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"231\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"239\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"256\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">2nd winter</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dens with mother</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"264\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">2nd spring</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">On its own</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Sows usually first breed at about 4, then every 2 to 3 years <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Few live past 15 to 20 in the wild <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: life history numbers</summary><ul><li>BC account <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>: females usually mature at about 4 years and breed every 2 to 3 years; where food is scarce, first litter at 6 or 7. Most males mature at 5 or 6. Captive bears live 25 to 30 years; wild bears usually much less.</li><li>WildSafeBC: over 30 years possible, 15 to 20 more typical; cub mortality around 50% <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Low birth rate means a population recovers slowly. That is why the law protects sows with young (Tip, my reading).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Body fact</th><th>So you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Heart low, lungs reach back (70 to 85%)</td><td>Halfway up, tight behind the shoulder</td></tr><tr><td>Fur hides the body (Tip)</td><td>Find the leg and elbow first</td></tr><tr><td>Thin blood trail (Tip)</td><td>Wait, then track slowly</td></tr><tr><td>Fat and hide hold heat <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td><td>Skin fast, cool fast</td></tr><tr><td>Trichinella in muscle <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td><td>Cook to 71°C (160°F)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Chapter 10 has the full shot to table plan.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Table of how a black bear body changes in the den. Heart rate drops from about 50 to 55 beats a minute to about 10 to 14. Metabolism drops to about 25 percent of normal. Body temperature falls only about 3 to 6 degrees Celsius. The bear does not eat, drink, urinate or defecate for months. It can lose up to a quarter of its body weight.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">In the den: the body slows down</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Summer</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Denned</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"74\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Heart</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50 to 55</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 to 14 a minute</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"116\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Metabolism</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 25%</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"158\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Body temp</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">normal</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 to 6 C lower</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"200\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eat, drink</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">yes</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">none for months</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"242\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weight</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fall peak</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a quarter lost</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Low heart, big lungs, tight to the leg.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 55 to 14: summer to den heartbeats a minute <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, echoing Alaska and Maryland agency advice): \"A bear's hide is a winter coat. Get it off the meat.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 25: metabolism in the den is about 25% of normal; a quarter of the weight is lost (80 to 90%).</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 4 and 2 to 3: a sow first breeds near 4, then every 2 to 3 years <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 20,000: fall calories a day <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Curved claws climb, straight claws dig.\"</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, from hunter education vitals advice): \"Wait for the near leg to step forward.\"</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Aiming at the middle of a fluffy bear.</li><li>Leaving a fall bear whole overnight in its hide.</li><li>Thinking a spring bear and a fall bear handle the same.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Before the hunt: study the <a href=\"#/s/black-bear\">vitals drawing</a> and point to the heart on three bear photos.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>BC Ministry of Environment, Lands and Parks (2001), <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/documents/blackbear.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Black Bears in British Columbia\"</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></li></ul><ul><li>ScienceDaily (17 February 2011), <a href=\"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2011/02/110217141311.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">hibernating black bears' metabolism</a>, on Tøien and others, Science 331:906, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Alaska Department of Fish and Game, <a href=\"https://www.adfg.alaska.gov/index.cfm?adfg=blackbear.main\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Black bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>WildSafeBC, <a href=\"https://wildsafebc.com/species/black-bear/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Black bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul><ul><li>North American Bear Center, <a href=\"https://bear.org/?p=53\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Senses and abilities</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Maryland Department of Natural Resources, <a href=\"https://dnr.maryland.gov/huntersguide/Pages/BearHunt_Care.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bear hunt: care of your bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul>","<ul><li>Virginia, <a href=\"https://dwr.ar.virginia.gov/wp-content/uploads/hunting-tips.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">hunting tips</a> adapted from the National Bowhunter Education Foundation, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Hunt Mentor lessons: <a href=\"#/s/black-bear\">Black bear</a>, <a href=\"#/s/shot-placement\">shot placement</a>.</li></ul><ul><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-black-bear.md</code>.</li></ul>"]